{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-104134" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-104134" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-104134" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b48a372790fc37c025de034462efbe04277ae345a801af901d5dcb0a718011b"} {"question" "q-104134" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-104134" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-104134" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-73485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-73485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -12 & -18 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 18 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-73485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b48a372790fc37c025de034462efbe04277ae345a801af901d5dcb0a718011b"} {"question" "q-73485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-73485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "12[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 12 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -18 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 18 \\\\ -12 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-73485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-9967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-9967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =4|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(-12+10)+2(32-35)+3(-16+21) \\\\  & =-8-6+15 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-9967" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b48a372790fc37c025de034462efbe04277ae345a801af901d5dcb0a718011b"} {"question" "q-9967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-9967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & -4 \\\\ 9 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-9967" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-319395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | $-1$ | $-3$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${A}^{-1}=\\,\\,$ {{field-2}} |  | $-1$ | $3$ | {{field-3}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-319395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =(-3)|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)(2-3)-0(\\,-2-(-3)\\,)+(-3+3) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/state.json" "file_sha256" "61f3e0f7297cb165d4eae2a6765b99446c040f0b5658df70520a6e1fe8d34b83"} {"question" "q-319395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7b48a372790fc37c025de034462efbe04277ae345a801af901d5dcb0a718011b"} {"question" "q-319395" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/139752